Europe benefits from rigorous Ecodesign directives that push manufacturers toward low‑loss magnetic components. German and French firms lead in integrating ferrite cores into industrial automation and renewable‑energy platforms.
Latin America sees growing demand from Brazil’s telecom expansion and renewable‑energy projects, though supply constraints keep pricing elevated.
Middle East & Africa exhibits a nuanced profile, with GCC countries prioritising high‑frequency power conversion for desalination and large‑scale solar installations, while sub‑Saharan markets adopt ferrite solutions to extend telecom reach under limited power budgets.
